From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:05:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] debian: Add nativehdr7 changelog entry

Summarise the gamut compression batch: ACES 1.3 Reference Gamut
Compression toward firmware-declared target primaries, following source
colors as pixels are converted, only for content that can exceed the
target, with limits exact over the source gamut boundary, the
declaration's per-primary resolution as the containment tolerance, the
nativehdr6 acceptance rule kept for client and EDID primaries, carried
by the rendering color state next to the target peak, and decided by
the single mapping predicate that also governs direct scanout and the
hardware cursor plane. The new exported symbols were added to the
symbols file with their commit, at 51.0-1ubuntu3+nativehdr7~.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
 debian/changelog | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index 9fa163d..41869c2 100644
--- a/debian/changelog
+++ b/debian/changelog
@@ -1,3 +1,36 @@
+mutter (51.0-1ubuntu3+nativehdr7) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium
+
+  * Compress colors outside a firmware-declared output target gamut with the
+    ACES 1.3 Reference Gamut Compression (threshold 0.8, power 1.2), in
+    linear RGB of the target primaries with absolute colorimetry, in the
+    surface to blending transform after highlight mapping. Source colors
+    are followed as the renderer converts them, white point adaptation to
+    D65 included. Only content that can exceed the target is compressed: a
+    bounded encoding must have a primary outside the target triangle, and
+    so must declared mastering primaries; content whose encoding fits the
+    target, such as sRGB on a wide gamut panel, never is. Extended-range
+    linear content is compressed only with declared mastering primaries,
+    which then bound it. Limits come from the mastering primaries when
+    declared, otherwise the encoding's, and are exact over the source gamut
+    boundary: no point of it, primaries or sides, ends beyond the target
+    boundary, and each channel's maximising point lands on it. Nothing is
+    compressed when the target primaries are the encoding fallback.
+  * Containment allows the resolution of the DisplayID declaration, per
+    primary (one 12-bit step in CIE 1931 xy, or its CIE 1976 equivalent at
+    that primary), carried with the target primaries, so content in the
+    declared gamut, such as P3 on a panel declaring P3, is not compressed
+    and keeps direct scanout.
+  * The rendering color state carries the firmware-declared target
+    primaries next to the target peak; display target primaries must also
+    pass an absolute matrix check, while client and EDID primaries keep the
+    nativehdr6 acceptance rule. Gamut compression is part of the single
+    mapping predicate, so direct scanout and the hardware cursor plane are
+    refused whenever it applies, and of the exact transform identity.
+  * KMS HDR metadata is unchanged. Source candidate only; runtime and
+    package qualification pending.
+
+ -- Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+
 mutter (51.0-1ubuntu3+nativehdr6) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium
 
   * Add the HLG transfer function (Rec. ITU-R BT.2100-2): decode with black
